)ATTR DEFAULT(@}_)
 @ TYPE(TEXT)   INTENS(HIGH) COLOR(WHITE)
 } TYPE(TEXT)   INTENS(LOW)  COLOR(GREEN)
 { TYPE(TEXT)   INTENS(LOW)  COLOR(TURQ)
 _ TYPE(INPUT)  INTENS(HIGH) COLOR(RED)    CAPS(ON) JUST(LEFT)
 ! TYPE(OUTPUT) INTENS(HIGH) COLOR(YELLOW) CAPS(OFF) JUST(LEFT)
)BODY
@HELP: Who May See and Do What                  !ISFHMSG                      }
@COMMAND INPUT ===>_ISFHCMD                                                   }
}  SDSF asks RAKF what you may see and do.
}
@  Your own jobs}, those that run under your user id, you always see, and
}  every action on them is allowed.
}
@  The jobs of others}are guarded by profiles of the RAKF class JESSPOOL.
}  The entity is owner.jobname.jobid, as in HERC02.PAYROLL.JOB01234.
{    READ    }The job is on the lists (ST, DA, I, O, H); D, L, ? and S.
{    UPDATE  }Also the other action characters and overtyping.
}  A job you may not read is not on the lists at all. An action you may
}  not take: NOT AUTHORIZED FOR JOB.
}
@  The system}is guarded by the FACILITY profile SDSF.OPER.
{    READ    }LOG, PR and INIT; on DA, the address spaces without a job;
}             D on a printer or an initiator.
{    UPDATE  }/ commands; the other actions on printers and initiators.
}  Without it: COMMAND NOT AUTHORIZED, NOT AUTHORIZED FOR CMD, PRT or INIT.
}
}  RAKF before 2.0.0 has no class JESSPOOL: then you see your own jobs only.
}
}
}  Enter: next page   PF7: contents   PF10: back   PF3: back to SDSF
)PROC
  &ISFHPFK = .PFKEY
  &ZCONT = ISFHAUT2
  &ZUP = ISFHTOC
)END
